      "number": "5.5.3",
      "text": "INTENTION:"
    },
    {
      "number": "5.5.3.9",
      "text": "A shim waking its device never takes more than 60 s. A sync caller waits at most 60 s for the wake, then gets \"not now\" back; a wake that misses 60 s is a trouble. 600 s is the limit for an inference call to come back, not for a wake."
    },
    {
      "number": "5.3.4",
      "text": "`cairn start` (= cairn cairn start) brings the system up: ground loop, bus, shims. `cairn stop` takes it down."
    },
